  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything yet. Removing `channel` from `OrderPlaced` goes against an architecture rule in this repo, so I'm checking with you first.\n\n**The conflict:** CLAUDE.md rule ARCH-4 says `OrderPlaced` is read by billing-service and analytics-ingest, which live in other repositories. It also says \"changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\" Deleting `channel` from the event is a removal. \"Nothing reads it anymore\" may well be true, but I can only search this repo, and nothing here confirms it.\n\n**What the full removal would involve:**\n- `src/core/events.ts:16,50`: remove the field from `OrderPlaced` and from `orderPlaced()`. This is the part ARCH-4 covers. It would also be a schema change, so `schemaVersion: 3` should probably go up to 4.\n- `src/core/order.ts`: remove `channel` from `Order` and `NewOrder`, plus `CHANNELS`, `Channel` and the validation at lines 124–125.\n- `src/api/requestParsing.ts:18,39-40`: stop reading `channel` from `POST /orders`. Clients that still send it would have it ignored rather than checked.\n- Tests in `test/app.test.ts`, `test/order.test.ts`, `test/helpers.ts` and `test/adapters.test.ts`, plus the examples in `README.md` and `CLAUDE.md`.\n\nThe order model is internal, and `GET /orders/{id}` doesn't return `channel`, so ARCH-8 isn't affected. The event field is the only blocker.\n\n**Options:**\n1. **Deprecate now, remove later (follows ARCH-4):** mark `OrderPlaced.channel` as `@deprecated` and keep publishing it. Once billing-service and analytics-ingest confirm they don't use it, a follow-up change removes it from the event, model, request parsing and tests.\n2. **Full removal now:** if the billing-service and analytics-ingest owners have already confirmed they don't read `channel`, or this already went through deprecation, tell me where that's recorded (a ticket or approval). I'll remove it everywhere listed above and bump the schema version.\n\nWhich do you want?",
